{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For the chief musician; happy is the one who considers</b> — this psalm is about his illness." "<b>Happy</b> — some say:" "<b>Considers</b> — like one who looks, like one who gazes [in] hif'il. And the correct [reading]: from the root שכל, that he set his mind to consider the deed of HaShem concerning the illness." "<b>And the poor</b> — in money and also in flesh, and it is the illness, as in: 'thus poor is the king's son.' Poverty and poor appearance." "And some say: that 'considers' — is a transitive verb, and it refers to the one who visits and speaks to his heart and instructs him." "And the meaning of <b>on a day of evil</b> — a supernal configuration opposite his birth." "<b>YHWH will deliver him</b> — alone, and not through the hand of man." "And the meaning of <b>will keep him</b> — that the illness not increase, and <b>will keep him alive</b>, for he fears death."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:28.488963853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}